k entity files remain source of truth. **Verified: cold rebuild 28.6s → snapshot boot 0.9s** (25MB gz from 282MB); delta replay survives restart; counts match full rebuild exactly. Test artifacts cleaned from data dir.\n\n**Git state:** both repos committed on branch **`perf/memoray-warm-index`** (NOT pushed): prime-silo `perf/memoray-warm-index` (Phase1 11f7557, Phase2 ec73ec0) + standalone memo-ray same branch (Phase1 f61c7db, Phase2 07686c9, files under `agent-os-dashboard/server/`). The two repos hold the SAME logic in different formatting (fork is prettier 2-space/double-quote; standalone is 4-space/single-quote) — mirror by re-applying edits per style, not patch-copy. Offered to push/PR; awaiting go.\n\n**Caveat:** `prime-silo/memoray` is a vendored fork (standalone memo-ray repo deliberately kept; fork may drift — see [[project_memoray_primesilo_merge]]). Land fixes here, mirror upstream. Also: packaged desktop build must be rebuilt/repackaged (devops-pipeline) for users to get this; running-from-source just needs a restart.\n\n**Backlog:**\n- **Phase 3** — shared **session drift ledger**","originalFile":"---\nname: prime_silo_memoray_startup_perf\ndescription: \"Why the Bridge memory views (mission control / session graph / pulse / lifelog) loaded slowly, and the Phase-1 incremental-store fix; Phase 2/3 backlog incl. LONGVIEW drift-ledger convergence\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 851718f5-23ec-463a-a795-8d103ace1c22\n  modified: 2026-07-20T18:05:48.062Z\n---\n\nThe Bridge \"memory\" screens (Mission Control, Session Graph, Pulse, Lifelog) are served by the **vendored memoray Express server** (`prime-silo/memoray/server/`), proxied via `/api/memoray` (`server/lib/memoray_proxy.js`, default 127.0.0.1:3030). Data store = `~/.mem0ray/data/entities/` — **measured 80,110 tiny JSON files / 282 MB** (one file per message/thought/tool-call block).\n\n**Diagnosis (2026-07-20):** session *parsing* was already delta-driven (mtime-gated per file — fine). The slowness was the read/cache path in `lib/entity_store.js`:\n- `load()` rebuilds the ENTIRE 80k-file Map from disk whenever `index.json` mtime changes. **Measured full rebuild ≈ 20–24s** on this machine (Windows, Defender).\n- All 4 parsers (`claude/antigravity/opencode/openNotebook Parser.js`) called `saveIndex()` **unconditionally every 30s** → mtime always bumped even with zero changes.\n- `performSync()` called `store.invalidate()` after every sync → warm cache thrown away.\n- Net: ~every 30s the next UI request paid a full 20s rebuild. Not \"reindex sessions on startup\" (parsing is delta) but \"rebuild the in-memory index constantly\" — same felt effect.\n\n**Phase 1 fix (SHIPPED to vendored fork, uncommitted):**\n- Each parser records written entity ids via new `store.recordTouched(id)` (only on actual write, respecting the skip-if-exists guard), and calls `saveIndex()` only when `touchedCount() > startTouched` (no change → no mtime bump → cache stays warm).\n- `performSync()` drains touched ids and calls new `store.applyDelta(ids)` (upsert just those into the warm Map, re-anchor `indexMtimeMs`) instead of `invalidate()`. ~3ms vs 20s.\n- `load()` now anchors to the mtime captured **after** the multi-second build, not before — prevents a mid-build index rewrite (two memoray procs sharing the data dir, or an in-process sync) from instantly re-staling the fresh cache and thrashing.\n- Phase-0 instrumentation left in: `[Store] Full rebuild: N entities in Xms` + per-sync `[Server] Delta sync: patched N / no changes / cache cold` logs.\n\n**Verified** single-process: load#1 cold 21s → load#2 warm **0ms** → applyDelta(5) **3ms** → subsequent loads **0ms**. Earlier apparent \"thrash\" in testing was a two-process confound (a test server on :3099 + the user's real app on :3030 both bumping the shared `index.json`) — NOT a logic bug.\n\n**Caveat:** `prime-silo/memoray` is a vendored fork (standalone memo-ray repo deliberately kept; fork may drift — see [[project_memoray_primesilo_merge]]). Land fixes here, mirror upstream.\n\n**Backlog (approved scope was Phase 0+1 only):**\n- **Phase 2** — persistent warm-index snapshot to kill the first-boot ~20s cold read (serialize the Map to one file; rebuild-from-loose-files only if missing/stale). Optional: consolidate the 80k loose files into one append store.\n- **Phase 3** — shared **session drift ledger** {path,size,mtime,content_hash,consumers:{memoray,longview}} so memoray + [[project_longview_session_synthesis]] stop double-indexing the same sessions; content-hash replaces memoray's fragile 5-min mtime buffer and distinguishes appended vs edited. The \"graph that grows\" the operator asked for; drift becomes a first-class signal that can drive incremental LONGVIEW top-ups.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: 851718f5-23ec-463a-a795-8d103ace1c22","-  modified: 2026-07-20T18:05:48.062Z","+  modified: 2026-07-20T19:05:37.138Z"," ---"," "," The Bridge \"memory\" screens (Mission Control, Session Graph, Pulse, Lifelog) are served by the **vendored memoray Express server** (`prime-silo/memoray/server/`), proxied via `/api/memoray` (`server/lib/memoray_proxy.js`, default 127.0.0.1:3030). Data store = `~/.mem0ray/data/entities/` — **measured 80,110 tiny JSON files / 282 MB** (one file per message/thought/tool-call block)."]},{"oldStart":24,"oldLines":8,"newStart":24,"newLines":11,"lines":[" "," **Verified** single-process: load#1 cold 21s → load#2 warm **0ms** → applyDelta(5) **3ms** → subsequent loads **0ms**. Earlier apparent \"thrash\" in testing was a two-process confound (a test server on :3099 + the user's real app on :3030 both bumping the shared `index.json`) — NOT a logic bug."," ","-**Caveat:** `prime-silo/memoray` is a vendored fork (standalone memo-ray repo deliberately kept; fork may drift — see [[project_memoray_primesilo_merge]]). Land fi